    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6C(4) Organisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6c-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing an\ninstrumentality of a State or Territory for the purposes of the\ndefinition of organisation in subsection (1), the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that the State or Territory has requested that the\ninstrumentality be prescribed for those purposes; and\n\n(b) consider:\n\n(i) whether treating the instrumentality as an organisation\nfor the purposes of this Act adversely affects the\ngovernment of the State or Territory; and\n\n(ii) the desirability of regulating under this Act the\ncollection, holding, use, correction, disclosure and\ntransfer of personal information by the instrumentality;\nand\n\n(iii) whether the law of the State or Territory regulates the\ncollection, holding, use, correction, disclosure and\ntransfer of personal information by the instrumentality\nto a standard that is at least equivalent to the standard\nthat would otherwise apply to the instrumentality under\nthis Act; and\n\n(c) consult the Commissioner about the matters mentioned in\nsubparagraphs (b)(ii) and (iii).\nState does not include Territory",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing an\ninstrumentality of a State or Territory for the purposes of the\ndefinition of organisation in subsection (1), the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that the State or Territory has requested that the\ninstrumentality be prescribed for those purposes; and\n\n(b) consider:\n\n(i) whether treating the instrumentality as an organisation\nfor the purposes of this Act adversely affects the\ngovernment of the State or Territory; and\n\n(ii) the desirability of regulating under this Act the\ncollection, holding, use, correction, disclosure and\ntransfer of personal information by the instrumentality;\nand\n\n(iii) whether the law of the State or Territory regulates the\ncollection, holding, use, correction, disclosure and\ntransfer of personal information by the instrumentality\nto a standard that is at least equivalent to the standard\nthat would otherwise apply to the instrumentality under\nthis Act; and\n\n(c) consult the Commissioner about the matters mentioned in\nsubparagraphs (b)(ii) and (iii).\nState does not include Territory",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6c-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6c-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "23d2ef4964296581ccdfdd4d015d3e756312f6ce598f582f4dabc0d751326660",
      "skos:note": "Minister must consult Commissioner before prescribing instrumentality for organisation purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
