      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(7) Paragraph (4)(c) does not prevent an individual, body corporate,\npartnership, unincorporated association or trust from being a small\nbusiness operator only because he, she or it discloses personal\ninformation about another individual:\n\n(a) with the consent of the other individual; or\n\n(b) as required or authorised by or under legislation.\nCollection with consent or under legislation",
      "skos:definition": "(7) Paragraph (4)(c) does not prevent an individual, body corporate,\npartnership, unincorporated association or trust from being a small\nbusiness operator only because he, she or it discloses personal\ninformation about another individual:\n\n(a) with the consent of the other individual; or\n\n(b) as required or authorised by or under legislation.\nCollection with consent or under legislation",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6d-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6d-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cb7d95d0bf9f67ac9d911bca6a31700e510c88fb4d27d0c7e7a479e40656cd1d",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of personal information is permitted with consent or under legislation."
    },
