    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6DA What is the annual turnover of a business?",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6da"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "What is the annual turnover of a business for a financial year?\n\n(1) The annual turnover of a business for a financial year is the total\nof the following that is earned in the year in the course of the\nbusiness:\n\n(a) the proceeds of sales of goods and/or services;\n\n(b) commission income;\n\n(c) repair and service income;\n\n(d) rent, leasing and hiring income;\n\n(e) government bounties and subsidies;\n\n(f) interest, royalties and dividends;\n\n(g) other operating income.\nNote:\nThe annual turnover for a financial year of a business carried on by an\nentity that does not carry on another business will often be similar to\nthe total of the instalment income the entity notifies to the\nCommissioner of Taxation for the 4 quarters in the year (or for the\nyear, if the entity pays tax in annual instalments).\n\n(2) However, if a business has been carried on for only part of a\nfinancial year, its annual turnover for the financial year is the\namount worked out using the formula:\nAmount that would be the\nannual turnover of the business\nunder subsection (1) if the part\nwere a whole financial year\nNumber of days in the\nwhole financial year\nNumber of days in the part\n×",
      "skos:definition": "What is the annual turnover of a business for a financial year?\n\n(1) The annual turnover of a business for a financial year is the total\nof the following that is earned in the year in the course of the\nbusiness:\n\n(a) the proceeds of sales of goods and/or services;\n\n(b) commission income;\n\n(c) repair and service income;\n\n(d) rent, leasing and hiring income;\n\n(e) government bounties and subsidies;\n\n(f) interest, royalties and dividends;\n\n(g) other operating income.\nNote:\nThe annual turnover for a financial year of a business carried on by an\nentity that does not carry on another business will often be similar to\nthe total of the instalment income the entity notifies to the\nCommissioner of Taxation for the 4 quarters in the year (or for the\nyear, if the entity pays tax in annual instalments).\n\n(2) However, if a business has been carried on for only part of a\nfinancial year, its annual turnover for the financial year is the\namount worked out using the formula:\nAmount that would be the\nannual turnover of the business\nunder subsection (1) if the part\nwere a whole financial year\nNumber of days in the\nwhole financial year\nNumber of days in the part\n×",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d553881ec30ee9f45fe275f1efbd4b1a9c12606ce89e0436d4f5c05c46eec70c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6da",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6DA What is the annual turnover of a business?",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "What is the annual turnover of a business for a financial year?\n\n(1) The annual turnover of a business for a financial year is the total\nof the following that is earned in the year in the course of the\nbusiness:\n\n(a) the proceeds of sales of goods and/or services;\n\n(b) commission income;\n\n(c) repair and service income;\n\n(d) rent, leasing and hiring income;\n\n(e) government bounties and subsidies;\n\n(f) interest, royalties and dividends;\n\n(g) other operating income.\nNote:\nThe annual turnover for a financial year of a business carried on by an\nentity that does not carry on another business will often be similar to\nthe total of the instalment income the entity notifies to the\nCommissioner of Taxation for the 4 quarters in the year (or for the\nyear, if the entity pays tax in annual instalments).\n\n(2) However, if a business has been carried on for only part of a\nfinancial year, its annual turnover for the financial year is the\namount worked out using the formula:\nAmount that would be the\nannual turnover of the business\nunder subsection (1) if the part\nwere a whole financial year\nNumber of days in the\nwhole financial year\nNumber of days in the part\n×"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6DA(1) What is the annual turnover of a business?",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6da-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The annual turnover of a business for a financial year is the total\nof the following that is earned in the year in the course of the\nbusiness:\n\n(a) the proceeds of sales of goods and/or services;\n\n(b) commission income;\n\n(c) repair and service income;\n\n(d) rent, leasing and hiring income;\n\n(e) government bounties and subsidies;\n\n(f) interest, royalties and dividends;\n\n(g) other operating income.\nNote:\nThe annual turnover for a financial year of a business carried on by an\nentity that does not carry on another business will often be similar to\nthe total of the instalment income the entity notifies to the\nCommissioner of Taxation for the 4 quarters in the year (or for the\nyear, if the entity pays tax in annual instalments).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The annual turnover of a business for a financial year is the total\nof the following that is earned in the year in the course of the\nbusiness:\n\n(a) the proceeds of sales of goods and/or services;\n\n(b) commission income;\n\n(c) repair and service income;\n\n(d) rent, leasing and hiring income;\n\n(e) government bounties and subsidies;\n\n(f) interest, royalties and dividends;\n\n(g) other operating income.\nNote:\nThe annual turnover for a financial year of a business carried on by an\nentity that does not carry on another business will often be similar to\nthe total of the instalment income the entity notifies to the\nCommissioner of Taxation for the 4 quarters in the year (or for the\nyear, if the entity pays tax in annual instalments).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "01b1a4fd5e0d08068e3fbdc52f37488230b823c52f05f92e625f63c95c310526",
      "skos:note": "Defines annual turnover of a business for tax purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6da-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6DA(1) What is the annual turnover of a business?",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The annual turnover of a business for a financial year is the total\nof the following that is earned in the year in the course of the\nbusiness:\n\n(a) the proceeds of sales of goods and/or services;\n\n(b) commission income;\n\n(c) repair and service income;\n\n(d) rent, leasing and hiring income;\n\n(e) government bounties and subsidies;\n\n(f) interest, royalties and dividends;\n\n(g) other operating income.\nNote:\nThe annual turnover for a financial year of a business carried on by an\nentity that does not carry on another business will often be similar to\nthe total of the instalment income the entity notifies to the\nCommissioner of Taxation for the 4 quarters in the year (or for the\nyear, if the entity pays tax in annual instalments)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-1-norm",
