    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6DA(2) What is the annual turnover of a business?",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6da-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, if a business has been carried on for only part of a\nfinancial year, its annual turnover for the financial year is the\namount worked out using the formula:\nAmount that would be the\nannual turnover of the business\nunder subsection (1) if the part\nwere a whole financial year\nNumber of days in the\nwhole financial year\nNumber of days in the part\n×",
      "skos:definition": "(2) However, if a business has been carried on for only part of a\nfinancial year, its annual turnover for the financial year is the\namount worked out using the formula:\nAmount that would be the\nannual turnover of the business\nunder subsection (1) if the part\nwere a whole financial year\nNumber of days in the\nwhole financial year\nNumber of days in the part\n×",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6da-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c89768810da8dc0e0feaaedd28fd491e9c105e57d69b523c73c1e29d012729ad",
      "skos:note": "Business must calculate annual turnover using a formula for partial financial years.",
      "dc:description": "Annual turnover calculation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6da-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6DA(2) What is the annual turnover of a business?",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, if a business has been carried on for only part of a\nfinancial year, its annual turnover for the financial year is the\namount worked out using the formula:\nAmount that would be the\nannual turnover of the business\nunder subsection (1) if the part\nwere a whole financial year\nNumber of days in the\nwhole financial year\nNumber of days in the part\n×"
    },
    {
