    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6e-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6E(4) Small business operator treated as organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6e-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing a\nsmall business operator, act or practice for the purposes of\nsubsection (1) or (2), the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that it is desirable in the public interest to\nregulate under this Act the small business operator, act or\npractice; and\n\n(b) consult the Commissioner about the desirability of regulating\nunder this Act the matters described in paragraph (a).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing a\nsmall business operator, act or practice for the purposes of\nsubsection (1) or (2), the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that it is desirable in the public interest to\nregulate under this Act the small business operator, act or\npractice; and\n\n(b) consult the Commissioner about the desirability of regulating\nunder this Act the matters described in paragraph (a).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6e"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6e-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6e-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ba620dccffafebc9cf748175514d35e4c896a445b85684929e8bc84b0852afbc",
      "skos:note": "Consultation requirement before regulating small business operator"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6e-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6E(4) Small business operator treated as organisation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing a\nsmall business operator, act or practice for the purposes of\nsubsection (1) or (2), the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that it is desirable in the public interest to\nregulate under this Act the small business operator, act or\npractice; and\n\n(b) consult the Commissioner about the desirability of regulating\nunder this Act the matters described in paragraph (a).\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6e-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
