    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6ea",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6EA Small business operators choosing to be treated as",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6ea"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "organisations\n\n(1) This Act (except section 16D) applies in relation to a small\nbusiness operator as if the operator were an organisation while a\nchoice by the operator to be treated as an organisation is registered\nunder this section.\n\n(2) A small business operator may make a choice in writing given to\nthe Commissioner to be treated as an organisation.\nNote:\nA small business operator may revoke such a choice by writing given\nto the Commissioner. See subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.\n\n(3) If the Commissioner is satisfied that a small business operator has\nmade the choice to be treated as an organisation, the Commissioner\nmust enter in a register of operators who have made such a choice:\n\n(a) the name or names under which the operator carries on\nbusiness; and\n\n(b) the operator’s ABN, if the operator has one under the A New\nTax System (Australian Business Number) Act 1999.\n\n(4) If a small business operator revokes a choice to be treated as an\norganisation, the Commissioner must remove from the register the\nmaterial relating to the operator.\n\n(5) The Commissioner may decide the form of the register and how it\nis to be kept.\n\n(6) The Commissioner must make the register available to the public\nin the way that the Commissioner determines. However, the\nCommissioner must not make available to the public in the register\ninformation other than that described in subsection (3).",
      "skos:definition": "organisations\n\n(1) This Act (except section 16D) applies in relation to a small\nbusiness operator as if the operator were an organisation while a\nchoice by the operator to be treated as an organisation is registered\nunder this section.\n\n(2) A small business operator may make a choice in writing given to\nthe Commissioner to be treated as an organisation.\nNote:\nA small business operator may revoke such a choice by writing given\nto the Commissioner. See subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.\n\n(3) If the Commissioner is satisfied that a small business operator has\nmade the choice to be treated as an organisation, the Commissioner\nmust enter in a register of operators who have made such a choice:\n\n(a) the name or names under which the operator carries on\nbusiness; and\n\n(b) the operator’s ABN, if the operator has one under the A New\nTax System (Australian Business Number) Act 1999.\n\n(4) If a small business operator revokes a choice to be treated as an\norganisation, the Commissioner must remove from the register the\nmaterial relating to the operator.\n\n(5) The Commissioner may decide the form of the register and how it\nis to be kept.\n\n(6) The Commissioner must make the register available to the public\nin the way that the Commissioner determines. However, the\nCommissioner must not make available to the public in the register\ninformation other than that described in subsection (3).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6ea-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6ea-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6ea-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6ea-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6ea-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6ea-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4471bc3dace330b3097080bd1d754d2485f6b99212f452d0674fda36b3f8160b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6ea",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6EA Small business operators choosing to be treated as",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "organisations\n\n(1) This Act (except section 16D) applies in relation to a small\nbusiness operator as if the operator were an organisation while a\nchoice by the operator to be treated as an organisation is registered\nunder this section.\n\n(2) A small business operator may make a choice in writing given to\nthe Commissioner to be treated as an organisation.\nNote:\nA small business operator may revoke such a choice by writing given\nto the Commissioner. See subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.\n\n(3) If the Commissioner is satisfied that a small business operator has\nmade the choice to be treated as an organisation, the Commissioner\nmust enter in a register of operators who have made such a choice:\n\n(a) the name or names under which the operator carries on\nbusiness; and\n\n(b) the operator’s ABN, if the operator has one under the A New\nTax System (Australian Business Number) Act 1999.\n\n(4) If a small business operator revokes a choice to be treated as an\norganisation, the Commissioner must remove from the register the\nmaterial relating to the operator.\n\n(5) The Commissioner may decide the form of the register and how it\nis to be kept.\n\n(6) The Commissioner must make the register available to the public\nin the way that the Commissioner determines. However, the\nCommissioner must not make available to the public in the register\ninformation other than that described in subsection (3)."
    },
