    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6f-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6F(3) State instrumentalities etc. treated as organisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6f-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing a State\nor Territory authority or instrumentality of a State or Territory for\nthe purposes of subsection (1), the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that the relevant State or Territory has requested\nthat the authority or instrumentality be prescribed for those\npurposes; and\n\n(b) consult the Commissioner about the desirability of regulating\nunder this Act the collection, holding, use, correction,\ndisclosure and transfer of personal information by the\nauthority or instrumentality.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing a State\nor Territory authority or instrumentality of a State or Territory for\nthe purposes of subsection (1), the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that the relevant State or Territory has requested\nthat the authority or instrumentality be prescribed for those\npurposes; and\n\n(b) consult the Commissioner about the desirability of regulating\nunder this Act the collection, holding, use, correction,\ndisclosure and transfer of personal information by the\nauthority or instrumentality.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6f"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6f-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6f-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-6f-ss-3-logic-epistemic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b70d1c01792809830a0d61b7d3567f124367aab52ed53e145926044e732c2da2",
      "skos:note": "Minister must consult Commissioner before prescribing State authority or instrumentality."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-6f-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6F(3) State instrumentalities etc. treated as organisations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Before the Governor-General makes regulations prescribing a State\nor Territory authority or instrumentality of a State or Territory for\nthe purposes of subsection (1), the Minister must:\n\n(a) be satisfied that the relevant State or Territory has requested\nthat the authority or instrumentality be prescribed for those\npurposes; and\n\n(b) consult the Commissioner about the desirability of regulating\nunder this Act the collection, holding, use, correction,\ndisclosure and transfer of personal information by the\nauthority or instrumentality."
    },
