    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-7b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7B(3) Exempt acts and exempt practices of organisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-7b-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(3) An act done, or practice engaged in, by an organisation that is or\nwas an employer of an individual, is exempt for the purposes of\nparagraph 7(1)(ee) if the act or practice is directly related to:\n\n(a) a current or former employment relationship between the\nemployer and the individual; and\n\n(b) an employee record held by the organisation and relating to\nthe individual.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\nJournalism",
      "skos:definition": "(3) An act done, or practice engaged in, by an organisation that is or\nwas an employer of an individual, is exempt for the purposes of\nparagraph 7(1)(ee) if the act or practice is directly related to:\n\n(a) a current or former employment relationship between the\nemployer and the individual; and\n\n(b) an employee record held by the organisation and relating to\nthe individual.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\nJournalism",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-7b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-7b-ss-3-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d6a340a228e6740a720740d4b424b590a2123931a703b4a62b1bce517f4aefa0",
      "skos:note": "Exempt acts and practices of organisations related to employment relationships."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-7b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7B(3) Exempt acts and exempt practices of organisations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "(3) An act done, or practice engaged in, by an organisation that is or\nwas an employer of an individual, is exempt for the purposes of\nparagraph 7(1)(ee) if the act or practice is directly related to:\n\n(a) a current or former employment relationship between the\nemployer and the individual; and\n\n(b) an employee record held by the organisation and relating to\nthe individual.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\nJournalism"
    },
    {
