    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-7c-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Exemption",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Agents or principals are exempt from the operation of the Act.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) Subsection (4) does not otherwise affect the operation of the Act in relation to agents or principals."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-7c-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7C(6) Political acts and practices are exempt",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-7c-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(6) In this section:\nelectoral law means a law of the Commonwealth, or a law of a\nState or Territory, relating to elections to a Parliament or to a local\ngovernment authority.\nParliament means:\n\n(a) the Parliament of the Commonwealth; or\n\n(b) a State Parliament; or\n\n(c) the legislature of a Territory.\nNote:\nTo avoid doubt, this section does not make exempt for the purposes of\nparagraph 7(1)(ee) an act or practice of the political representative,\ncontractor, subcontractor or volunteer for a registered political party\ninvolving the use or disclosure (by way of sale or otherwise) of\npersonal information in a way not covered by subsection (1), (2), (3)\nor (4) (as appropriate). The rest of this Act operates normally in\nrelation to that act or practice.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) In this section:\nelectoral law means a law of the Commonwealth, or a law of a\nState or Territory, relating to elections to a Parliament or to a local\ngovernment authority.\nParliament means:\n\n(a) the Parliament of the Commonwealth; or\n\n(b) a State Parliament; or\n\n(c) the legislature of a Territory.\nNote:\nTo avoid doubt, this section does not make exempt for the purposes of\nparagraph 7(1)(ee) an act or practice of the political representative,\ncontractor, subcontractor or volunteer for a registered political party\ninvolving the use or disclosure (by way of sale or otherwise) of\npersonal information in a way not covered by subsection (1), (2), (3)\nor (4) (as appropriate). The rest of this Act operates normally in\nrelation to that act or practice.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-7c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-7c-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-7c-ss-6-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-7c-ss-6-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "37af4feca2ebb7aba6e79c00331451104f5faa81d28b921bec84e0c388f64add",
      "skos:note": "Electoral law and Parliament definitions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-7c-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7C(6) Political acts and practices are exempt",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(6) In this section:\nelectoral law means a law of the Commonwealth, or a law of a\nState or Territory, relating to elections to a Parliament or to a local\ngovernment authority.\nParliament means:\n\n(a) the Parliament of the Commonwealth; or\n\n(b) a State Parliament; or\n\n(c) the legislature of a Territory.\nNote:\nTo avoid doubt, this section does not make exempt for the purposes of\nparagraph 7(1)(ee) an act or practice of the political representative,\ncontractor, subcontractor or volunteer for a registered political party\ninvolving the use or disclosure (by way of sale or otherwise) of\npersonal information in a way not covered by subsection (1), (2), (3)\nor (4) (as appropriate). The rest of this Act operates normally in\nrelation to that act or practice."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-7c-ss-6-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
