    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-12b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12B(2) Severability: additional effect of Act in relation to organisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-12b-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(2) This Act also has the effect it would have if its operation in relation\nto organisations were expressly confined to an operation to give\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\neffect to the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights,\nand in particular Article 17 of the Covenant.\nNote:\nThe text of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights is\nset out in Australian Treaty Series 1980 No. 23. In 2000, this was\navailable in the Australian Treaties Library of the Department of\nForeign Affairs and Trade, accessible on the Internet through that\nDepartment’s world-wide web site.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) This Act also has the effect it would have if its operation in relation\nto organisations were expressly confined to an operation to give\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\neffect to the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights,\nand in particular Article 17 of the Covenant.\nNote:\nThe text of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights is\nset out in Australian Treaty Series 1980 No. 23. In 2000, this was\navailable in the Australian Treaties Library of the Department of\nForeign Affairs and Trade, accessible on the Internet through that\nDepartment’s world-wide web site.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-12b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-12b-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-12b-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4acb2b6fd678efd9c3e15caa8f2df0615c46ca8264efeb3463e13785f1518872",
      "skos:note": "Act has effect on International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-12b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12B(2) Severability: additional effect of Act in relation to organisations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(2) This Act also has the effect it would have if its operation in relation\nto organisations were expressly confined to an operation to give\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\neffect to the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights,\nand in particular Article 17 of the Covenant.\nNote:\nThe text of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights is\nset out in Australian Treaty Series 1980 No. 23. In 2000, this was\navailable in the Australian Treaties Library of the Department of\nForeign Affairs and Trade, accessible on the Internet through that\nDepartment’s world-wide web site."
    },
