      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) However, paragraph (1)(a) does not apply to the collection by a\nbody corporate of personal information (other than sensitive\ninformation) from:\n\n(a) a related body corporate that is not an organisation; or\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(b) a related body corporate whose disclosure of the information\nto the body corporate is an exempt act or exempt practice for\nthe purposes of paragraph 7(1)(ee); or\n\n(c) a related body corporate whose disclosure of the information\nto the body corporate is not an interference with privacy\nbecause of section 13D.\nNote:\nThe effect of subsection (1A) is that a body corporate’s failure to\ncomply with the National Privacy Principles, or a binding approved\nprivacy code, in collecting personal information about an individual\nfrom a related body corporate covered by that subsection is an\ninterference with the privacy of the individual.\nRelationship with paragraphs 13A(1)(c) and (d)",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) However, paragraph (1)(a) does not apply to the collection by a\nbody corporate of personal information (other than sensitive\ninformation) from:\n\n(a) a related body corporate that is not an organisation; or\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(b) a related body corporate whose disclosure of the information\nto the body corporate is an exempt act or exempt practice for\nthe purposes of paragraph 7(1)(ee); or\n\n(c) a related body corporate whose disclosure of the information\nto the body corporate is not an interference with privacy\nbecause of section 13D.\nNote:\nThe effect of subsection (1A) is that a body corporate’s failure to\ncomply with the National Privacy Principles, or a binding approved\nprivacy code, in collecting personal information about an individual\nfrom a related body corporate covered by that subsection is an\ninterference with the privacy of the individual.\nRelationship with paragraphs 13A(1)(c) and (d)",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-13b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-13b-ss-1a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-13b-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "307d9aa1adde350ca3616b6548c46f9f5b3170946db8f48eb0178ad00c327f03",
      "skos:note": "Exempt disclosure of personal information from related body corporate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-13b-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13B(1A) Related bodies corporate",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) However, paragraph (1)(a) does not apply to the collection by a\nbody corporate of personal information (other than sensitive\ninformation) from:\n\n(a) a related body corporate that is not an organisation; or\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(b) a related body corporate whose disclosure of the information\nto the body corporate is an exempt act or exempt practice for\nthe purposes of paragraph 7(1)(ee); or\n\n(c) a related body corporate whose disclosure of the information\nto the body corporate is not an interference with privacy\nbecause of section 13D.\nNote:\nThe effect of subsection (1A) is that a body corporate’s failure to\ncomply with the National Privacy Principles, or a binding approved\nprivacy code, in collecting personal information about an individual\nfrom a related body corporate covered by that subsection is an\ninterference with the privacy of the individual.\nRelationship with paragraphs 13A(1)(c) and (d)"
    },
    {
