    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-13d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "13D Overseas act required by foreign law",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-13d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "Acts or practices that are not interferences with privacy\n\n(1) An act or practice of an organisation done or engaged in outside\nAustralia and an external Territory is not an interference with the\nprivacy of an individual if the act or practice is required by an\napplicable law of a foreign country.\nEffect despite section 13A\n\n(2) Subsection (1) has effect despite section 13A.",
      "skos:definition": "Acts or practices that are not interferences with privacy\n\n(1) An act or practice of an organisation done or engaged in outside\nAustralia and an external Territory is not an interference with the\nprivacy of an individual if the act or practice is required by an\napplicable law of a foreign country.\nEffect despite section 13A\n\n(2) Subsection (1) has effect despite section 13A.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-13d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-13d-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0a4e24f96c6620a4f17f1a745c4a1b39c1f0dac01c086e388a6bf1c0c6978488"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-13d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "13D Overseas act required by foreign law",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "Acts or practices that are not interferences with privacy\n\n(1) An act or practice of an organisation done or engaged in outside\nAustralia and an external Territory is not an interference with the\nprivacy of an individual if the act or practice is required by an\napplicable law of a foreign country.\nEffect despite section 13A\n\n(2) Subsection (1) has effect despite section 13A."
    },
    {
