    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-16a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16A Organisations to comply with approved privacy codes or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-16a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "National Privacy Principles\n\n(1) An organisation must not do an act, or engage in a practice, that\nbreaches an approved privacy code that binds the organisation.\n\n(2) To the extent (if any) that an organisation is not bound by an\napproved privacy code, the organisation must not do an act, or\nengage in a practice, that breaches a National Privacy Principle.\n\n(3) This section, approved privacy codes and the National Privacy\nPrinciples have effect in addition to sections 18 and 18A and",
      "skos:definition": "National Privacy Principles\n\n(1) An organisation must not do an act, or engage in a practice, that\nbreaches an approved privacy code that binds the organisation.\n\n(2) To the extent (if any) that an organisation is not bound by an\napproved privacy code, the organisation must not do an act, or\nengage in a practice, that breaches a National Privacy Principle.\n\n(3) This section, approved privacy codes and the National Privacy\nPrinciples have effect in addition to sections 18 and 18A and",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-16a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-16a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-16a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bde30ff1d48af8e724477e1ef36d82775637ce3f68d2a6eb0512424453e05a35"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-16a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16A Organisations to comply with approved privacy codes or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "National Privacy Principles\n\n(1) An organisation must not do an act, or engage in a practice, that\nbreaches an approved privacy code that binds the organisation.\n\n(2) To the extent (if any) that an organisation is not bound by an\napproved privacy code, the organisation must not do an act, or\nengage in a practice, that breaches a National Privacy Principle.\n\n(3) This section, approved privacy codes and the National Privacy\nPrinciples have effect in addition to sections 18 and 18A and"
    },
