    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-18be",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18BE Revoking the approval of an approved privacy code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-18be"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may revoke his or her approval of an approved\nprivacy code or a variation of an approved privacy code:\n\n(a) on his or her own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application by an organisation that is bound by the code.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(2) Before deciding whether to revoke the approval of a code or\nvariation, the Commissioner must:\n\n(a) if practicable, consult the organisation that originally sought\napproval of the code or variation; and\n\n(b) consult any other person the Commissioner considers\nappropriate; and\n\n(c) consider the extent to which members of the public have\nbeen given an opportunity to comment on the proposed\nrevocation.\n\n(3) A revocation must be in writing.\n\n(4) A revocation comes into effect on the day specified in the\nrevocation.\n\n(5) The day specified must not be before the day on which the\nrevocation is made.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may revoke his or her approval of an approved\nprivacy code or a variation of an approved privacy code:\n\n(a) on his or her own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application by an organisation that is bound by the code.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(2) Before deciding whether to revoke the approval of a code or\nvariation, the Commissioner must:\n\n(a) if practicable, consult the organisation that originally sought\napproval of the code or variation; and\n\n(b) consult any other person the Commissioner considers\nappropriate; and\n\n(c) consider the extent to which members of the public have\nbeen given an opportunity to comment on the proposed\nrevocation.\n\n(3) A revocation must be in writing.\n\n(4) A revocation comes into effect on the day specified in the\nrevocation.\n\n(5) The day specified must not be before the day on which the\nrevocation is made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-18be-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-18be-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-18be-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-18be-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-18be-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cee9db690a1645451b6d21650a07dcdbbb232714eb4353a2ee41ee2299493763"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-18be",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18BE Revoking the approval of an approved privacy code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may revoke his or her approval of an approved\nprivacy code or a variation of an approved privacy code:\n\n(a) on his or her own initiative; or\n\n(b) on application by an organisation that is bound by the code.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(2) Before deciding whether to revoke the approval of a code or\nvariation, the Commissioner must:\n\n(a) if practicable, consult the organisation that originally sought\napproval of the code or variation; and\n\n(b) consult any other person the Commissioner considers\nappropriate; and\n\n(c) consider the extent to which members of the public have\nbeen given an opportunity to comment on the proposed\nrevocation.\n\n(3) A revocation must be in writing.\n\n(4) A revocation comes into effect on the day specified in the\nrevocation.\n\n(5) The day specified must not be before the day on which the\nrevocation is made."
    },
