      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-18bi",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18BI Review of adjudicator’s decision under approved privacy code",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-18bi"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.48",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who is aggrieved by a determination made by an\nadjudicator (other than the Commissioner) under an approved\nprivacy code after investigating a complaint may apply to the\nCommissioner for review of the determination.\nNote:\nThe review of the adjudicator’s determination will include review of\nany finding, declaration, order or direction that is included in the\ndetermination.\n\n(2) Divisions 1 and 2 of Part V apply in relation to the complaint\ncovered by the application as if the complaint had been made to the\nCommissioner and subsection 36(1A) did not prevent the\nCommissioner from investigating it.\nNote:\nDivisions 1 and 2 of Part V provide for the investigation and\ndetermination of complaints made to the Commissioner.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(3) The adjudicator’s determination continues to have effect unless and\nuntil the Commissioner makes a determination under Division 2 of\nPart V relating to the complaint.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person who is aggrieved by a determination made by an\nadjudicator (other than the Commissioner) under an approved\nprivacy code after investigating a complaint may apply to the\nCommissioner for review of the determination.\nNote:\nThe review of the adjudicator’s determination will include review of\nany finding, declaration, order or direction that is included in the\ndetermination.\n\n(2) Divisions 1 and 2 of Part V apply in relation to the complaint\ncovered by the application as if the complaint had been made to the\nCommissioner and subsection 36(1A) did not prevent the\nCommissioner from investigating it.\nNote:\nDivisions 1 and 2 of Part V provide for the investigation and\ndetermination of complaints made to the Commissioner.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(3) The adjudicator’s determination continues to have effect unless and\nuntil the Commissioner makes a determination under Division 2 of\nPart V relating to the complaint.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-18bi-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-18bi-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-18bi-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2b202db470f017c1341425bb19a3fbf29e7d94bafb09468b38bde727c9eeb452"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-18bi",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18BI Review of adjudicator’s decision under approved privacy code",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 48,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who is aggrieved by a determination made by an\nadjudicator (other than the Commissioner) under an approved\nprivacy code after investigating a complaint may apply to the\nCommissioner for review of the determination.\nNote:\nThe review of the adjudicator’s determination will include review of\nany finding, declaration, order or direction that is included in the\ndetermination.\n\n(2) Divisions 1 and 2 of Part V apply in relation to the complaint\ncovered by the application as if the complaint had been made to the\nCommissioner and subsection 36(1A) did not prevent the\nCommissioner from investigating it.\nNote:\nDivisions 1 and 2 of Part V provide for the investigation and\ndetermination of complaints made to the Commissioner.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(3) The adjudicator’s determination continues to have effect unless and\nuntil the Commissioner makes a determination under Division 2 of\nPart V relating to the complaint."
    },
    {
