      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(ea) to prepare, and to publish in the way that the Commissioner\nconsiders appropriate, guidelines:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(i) to assist organisations to develop privacy codes or to\napply approved privacy codes; or\n\n(ii) relating to making and dealing with complaints under\napproved privacy codes; or\n\n(iii) about matters the Commissioner may consider in\ndeciding whether to approve a privacy code or a\nvariation of an approved privacy code;",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(ea) to prepare, and to publish in the way that the Commissioner\nconsiders appropriate, guidelines:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(i) to assist organisations to develop privacy codes or to\napply approved privacy codes; or\n\n(ii) relating to making and dealing with complaints under\napproved privacy codes; or\n\n(iii) about matters the Commissioner may consider in\ndeciding whether to approve a privacy code or a\nvariation of an approved privacy code;",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-63-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a72a36c2ac91fb8ff5affec9dc1f90a68e51be5f921222f5fe72c902bc2490f8",
      "skos:note": "Insert guidelines for preparing and publishing privacy codes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-63",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63 After paragraph 27(1)(e)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(ea) to prepare, and to publish in the way that the Commissioner\nconsiders appropriate, guidelines:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(i) to assist organisations to develop privacy codes or to\napply approved privacy codes; or\n\n(ii) relating to making and dealing with complaints under\napproved privacy codes; or\n\n(iii) about matters the Commissioner may consider in\ndeciding whether to approve a privacy code or a\nvariation of an approved privacy code;"
    },
