    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-74",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "74 After subsection 36(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-74"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) Subsection (1) does not apply to a complaint by an individual\nabout an act or practice of an organisation that is bound by an\napproved privacy code that:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(a) contains a procedure for making and dealing with complaints\nto an adjudicator in relation to acts or practices that may be\nan interference with the privacy of an individual; and\n\n(b) is relevant to the act or practice complained of.\n\n(1B) Subsection (1A) does not prevent an individual from making a\ncomplaint under an approved privacy code to the adjudicator for\nthe code if the adjudicator is the Commissioner.\n\n(1C) Subsection (1A) does not prevent an individual from complaining\nunder this Part to the Commissioner about an act done, or practice\nengaged in, by an organisation purportedly for the purpose of\nmeeting (directly or indirectly) an obligation under a\nCommonwealth contract (whether or not the organisation is a party\nto the contract).\nNote:\nSection 40A requires an adjudicator for an approved privacy code to\nrefer a code complaint to the Commissioner if the complaint is about\nan act or practice of a contracted service provider for a\nCommonwealth contract.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(1A) Subsection (1) does not apply to a complaint by an individual\nabout an act or practice of an organisation that is bound by an\napproved privacy code that:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(a) contains a procedure for making and dealing with complaints\nto an adjudicator in relation to acts or practices that may be\nan interference with the privacy of an individual; and\n\n(b) is relevant to the act or practice complained of.\n\n(1B) Subsection (1A) does not prevent an individual from making a\ncomplaint under an approved privacy code to the adjudicator for\nthe code if the adjudicator is the Commissioner.\n\n(1C) Subsection (1A) does not prevent an individual from complaining\nunder this Part to the Commissioner about an act done, or practice\nengaged in, by an organisation purportedly for the purpose of\nmeeting (directly or indirectly) an obligation under a\nCommonwealth contract (whether or not the organisation is a party\nto the contract).\nNote:\nSection 40A requires an adjudicator for an approved privacy code to\nrefer a code complaint to the Commissioner if the complaint is about\nan act or practice of a contracted service provider for a\nCommonwealth contract.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-74-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-74-ss-1b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-74-ss-1c"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-74",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "74 After subsection 36(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) Subsection (1) does not apply to a complaint by an individual\nabout an act or practice of an organisation that is bound by an\napproved privacy code that:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(a) contains a procedure for making and dealing with complaints\nto an adjudicator in relation to acts or practices that may be\nan interference with the privacy of an individual; and\n\n(b) is relevant to the act or practice complained of.\n\n(1B) Subsection (1A) does not prevent an individual from making a\ncomplaint under an approved privacy code to the adjudicator for\nthe code if the adjudicator is the Commissioner.\n\n(1C) Subsection (1A) does not prevent an individual from complaining\nunder this Part to the Commissioner about an act done, or practice\nengaged in, by an organisation purportedly for the purpose of\nmeeting (directly or indirectly) an obligation under a\nCommonwealth contract (whether or not the organisation is a party\nto the contract).\nNote:\nSection 40A requires an adjudicator for an approved privacy code to\nrefer a code complaint to the Commissioner if the complaint is about\nan act or practice of a contracted service provider for a\nCommonwealth contract."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-74-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "74(1A) After subsection 36(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-74-ss-1a"
      },
