        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bcc3e1addf773a2cdd1d35577a29cf5fe6e62aa1ac10fbcb06158b328553943c",
      "skos:note": "Exemption for organisations bound by approved privacy code"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-74-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "74(1A) After subsection 36(1)",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) Subsection (1) does not apply to a complaint by an individual\nabout an act or practice of an organisation that is bound by an\napproved privacy code that:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(a) contains a procedure for making and dealing with complaints\nto an adjudicator in relation to acts or practices that may be\nan interference with the privacy of an individual; and\n\n(b) is relevant to the act or practice complained of."
    },
