    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80 After subsection 40(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-80"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) The Commissioner must not investigate a complaint if the\ncomplainant did not complain to the respondent before making the\ncomplaint to the Commissioner under section 36. However, the\nCommissioner may decide to investigate the complaint if he or she\nconsiders that it was not appropriate for the complainant to\ncomplain to the respondent.\n\n(1B) The Commissioner must investigate under this Part a complaint\nabout an act or practice of an organisation that is bound by a\nrelevant approved privacy code that contains a procedure for\nmaking and dealing with complaints in relation to acts or practices\nthat may be an interference with the privacy of an individual if:\n\n(a) the act or practice occurred after the approval of the code\ncame into effect; and\n\n(b) the adjudicator for the code refers the complaint to the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(c) the Commissioner accepts the complaint; and\n\n(d) the Commissioner consults the complainant before accepting\nthe complaint.\n\n(1C) If the Commissioner accepts a complaint mentioned in\nsubsection (1B), the Commissioner must deal with it as if it were a\ncomplaint made under section 36 in relation to an act or practice of\nthe organisation.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(1A) The Commissioner must not investigate a complaint if the\ncomplainant did not complain to the respondent before making the\ncomplaint to the Commissioner under section 36. However, the\nCommissioner may decide to investigate the complaint if he or she\nconsiders that it was not appropriate for the complainant to\ncomplain to the respondent.\n\n(1B) The Commissioner must investigate under this Part a complaint\nabout an act or practice of an organisation that is bound by a\nrelevant approved privacy code that contains a procedure for\nmaking and dealing with complaints in relation to acts or practices\nthat may be an interference with the privacy of an individual if:\n\n(a) the act or practice occurred after the approval of the code\ncame into effect; and\n\n(b) the adjudicator for the code refers the complaint to the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(c) the Commissioner accepts the complaint; and\n\n(d) the Commissioner consults the complainant before accepting\nthe complaint.\n\n(1C) If the Commissioner accepts a complaint mentioned in\nsubsection (1B), the Commissioner must deal with it as if it were a\ncomplaint made under section 36 in relation to an act or practice of\nthe organisation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80-ss-1b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80-ss-1c"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-80",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80 After subsection 40(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) The Commissioner must not investigate a complaint if the\ncomplainant did not complain to the respondent before making the\ncomplaint to the Commissioner under section 36. However, the\nCommissioner may decide to investigate the complaint if he or she\nconsiders that it was not appropriate for the complainant to\ncomplain to the respondent.\n\n(1B) The Commissioner must investigate under this Part a complaint\nabout an act or practice of an organisation that is bound by a\nrelevant approved privacy code that contains a procedure for\nmaking and dealing with complaints in relation to acts or practices\nthat may be an interference with the privacy of an individual if:\n\n(a) the act or practice occurred after the approval of the code\ncame into effect; and\n\n(b) the adjudicator for the code refers the complaint to the\nCommissioner; and\n\n(c) the Commissioner accepts the complaint; and\n\n(d) the Commissioner consults the complainant before accepting\nthe complaint.\n\n(1C) If the Commissioner accepts a complaint mentioned in\nsubsection (1B), the Commissioner must deal with it as if it were a\ncomplaint made under section 36 in relation to an act or practice of\nthe organisation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80(1A) After subsection 40(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-80-ss-1a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) The Commissioner must not investigate a complaint if the\ncomplainant did not complain to the respondent before making the\ncomplaint to the Commissioner under section 36. However, the\nCommissioner may decide to investigate the complaint if he or she\nconsiders that it was not appropriate for the complainant to\ncomplain to the respondent.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) The Commissioner must not investigate a complaint if the\ncomplainant did not complain to the respondent before making the\ncomplaint to the Commissioner under section 36. However, the\nCommissioner may decide to investigate the complaint if he or she\nconsiders that it was not appropriate for the complainant to\ncomplain to the respondent.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80-ss-1a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ee964b88e9b301de2db70ae794b45e3df9ba74a43e2d9ac152d5e8430d7edf34",
      "skos:note": "Commissioner must not investigate complaint if complainant did not complain to respondent first."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-80-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80(1A) After subsection 40(1)",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) The Commissioner must not investigate a complaint if the\ncomplainant did not complain to the respondent before making the\ncomplaint to the Commissioner under section 36. However, the\nCommissioner may decide to investigate the complaint if he or she\nconsiders that it was not appropriate for the complainant to\ncomplain to the respondent."
    },
