      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) Before starting to investigate an act done, or practice engaged in,\nby a contracted service provider for the purpose of providing\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(directly or indirectly) a service to an agency under a\nCommonwealth contract, the Commissioner must also inform the\nagency that the act or practice is to be investigated.\nNote:\nSee subsection 6(9) about provision of services to an agency.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(1A) Before starting to investigate an act done, or practice engaged in,\nby a contracted service provider for the purpose of providing\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(directly or indirectly) a service to an agency under a\nCommonwealth contract, the Commissioner must also inform the\nagency that the act or practice is to be investigated.\nNote:\nSee subsection 6(9) about provision of services to an agency.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-89-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-89-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bb09cfc5894fdcaf1a19af4276cbc6cacd1ae9609369e06e8b9888a88b01b9db",
      "skos:note": "Agency must be informed of investigation into act or practice by contracted service provider."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-89",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "89 After subsection 43(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) Before starting to investigate an act done, or practice engaged in,\nby a contracted service provider for the purpose of providing\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(directly or indirectly) a service to an agency under a\nCommonwealth contract, the Commissioner must also inform the\nagency that the act or practice is to be investigated.\nNote:\nSee subsection 6(9) about provision of services to an agency."
    },
