    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-91",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "91 After subsection 43(8)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-91"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(8A) Subsection (8) does not allow the Commissioner to discuss a\nmatter relevant to an investigation of a breach of an approved\nprivacy code or the National Privacy Principles with a Minister,\nunless the investigation is of an act done, or practice engaged in:\n\n(a) by a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth\ncontract; and\n\n(b) for the purpose of providing a service to an agency to meet\n(directly or indirectly) an obligation under the contract.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(8A) Subsection (8) does not allow the Commissioner to discuss a\nmatter relevant to an investigation of a breach of an approved\nprivacy code or the National Privacy Principles with a Minister,\nunless the investigation is of an act done, or practice engaged in:\n\n(a) by a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth\ncontract; and\n\n(b) for the purpose of providing a service to an agency to meet\n(directly or indirectly) an obligation under the contract.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-91-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-91-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-91-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-91-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-91-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e2651b071046b8b4f7308d15bd04313516c5a0faccf1612ba80a27e4c03e9998",
      "skos:note": "The Commissioner is not allowed to discuss a matter relevant to an investigation of a breach of an approved privacy code or the National Privacy Principles with a Minister, unless certain conditions are met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-91",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "91 After subsection 43(8)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(8A) Subsection (8) does not allow the Commissioner to discuss a\nmatter relevant to an investigation of a breach of an approved\nprivacy code or the National Privacy Principles with a Minister,\nunless the investigation is of an act done, or practice engaged in:\n\n(a) by a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth\ncontract; and\n\n(b) for the purpose of providing a service to an agency to meet\n(directly or indirectly) an obligation under the contract."
    },
