    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-53a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53A Notice to be given to outsourcing agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-53a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commissioner makes a determination to which a contracted\nservice provider for a Commonwealth contract is the respondent,\nthe Commissioner:\n\n(a) must give a copy of the determination to each agency:\n\n(i) to which services are or were to be provided under the\ncontract; and\n\n(ii) to which the Commissioner considers it appropriate to\ngive a copy; and\n\n(b) may give such an agency a written recommendation of any\nmeasures that the Commissioner considers appropriate.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may give an agency a recommendation only\nafter consulting the agency.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(3) An agency that receives a recommendation from the Commissioner\nmust tell the Commissioner in writing of any action the agency\nproposes to take in relation to the recommendation. The agency\nmust do so within 60 days of receiving the recommendation.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Commissioner makes a determination to which a contracted\nservice provider for a Commonwealth contract is the respondent,\nthe Commissioner:\n\n(a) must give a copy of the determination to each agency:\n\n(i) to which services are or were to be provided under the\ncontract; and\n\n(ii) to which the Commissioner considers it appropriate to\ngive a copy; and\n\n(b) may give such an agency a written recommendation of any\nmeasures that the Commissioner considers appropriate.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may give an agency a recommendation only\nafter consulting the agency.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(3) An agency that receives a recommendation from the Commissioner\nmust tell the Commissioner in writing of any action the agency\nproposes to take in relation to the recommendation. The agency\nmust do so within 60 days of receiving the recommendation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-53a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-53a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-53a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c92e399d6ea1fc06f40aa72a551e237612ea3025a42ea50da85b86c5da705eae"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-53a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53A Notice to be given to outsourcing agency",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Commissioner makes a determination to which a contracted\nservice provider for a Commonwealth contract is the respondent,\nthe Commissioner:\n\n(a) must give a copy of the determination to each agency:\n\n(i) to which services are or were to be provided under the\ncontract; and\n\n(ii) to which the Commissioner considers it appropriate to\ngive a copy; and\n\n(b) may give such an agency a written recommendation of any\nmeasures that the Commissioner considers appropriate.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may give an agency a recommendation only\nafter consulting the agency.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(3) An agency that receives a recommendation from the Commissioner\nmust tell the Commissioner in writing of any action the agency\nproposes to take in relation to the recommendation. The agency\nmust do so within 60 days of receiving the recommendation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-53a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53A(1) Notice to be given to outsourcing agency",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-53a-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
