    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-55b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55B Evidentiary certificate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-55b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may issue a written certificate setting out the\nfindings of fact upon which the Commissioner based his or her\ndetermination that:\n\n(a) a specified agency had breached an Information Privacy\nPrinciple; or\n\n(b) a specified organisation had breached an approved privacy\ncode or a National Privacy Principle.\n\n(2) An adjudicator for an approved privacy code may issue a written\ncertificate setting out the findings of fact upon which the\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\nadjudicator based his or her determination that a specified\norganisation had breached an approved privacy code.\n\n(3) In any proceedings under section 55A, a certificate under\nsubsection (1) or (2) of this section is prima facie evidence of the\nfacts found by the Commissioner or adjudicator and set out in the\ncertificate. However, the certificate is not prima facie evidence of a\nfinding that:\n\n(a) a specified agency had breached an Information Privacy\nPrinciple; or\n\n(b) a specified organisation had breached an approved privacy\ncode or a National Privacy Principle.\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate under subsection (1) or (2)\nmust, unless the contrary is established, be taken to be a certificate\nand to have been properly given.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commissioner may issue a written certificate setting out the\nfindings of fact upon which the Commissioner based his or her\ndetermination that:\n\n(a) a specified agency had breached an Information Privacy\nPrinciple; or\n\n(b) a specified organisation had breached an approved privacy\ncode or a National Privacy Principle.\n\n(2) An adjudicator for an approved privacy code may issue a written\ncertificate setting out the findings of fact upon which the\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\nadjudicator based his or her determination that a specified\norganisation had breached an approved privacy code.\n\n(3) In any proceedings under section 55A, a certificate under\nsubsection (1) or (2) of this section is prima facie evidence of the\nfacts found by the Commissioner or adjudicator and set out in the\ncertificate. However, the certificate is not prima facie evidence of a\nfinding that:\n\n(a) a specified agency had breached an Information Privacy\nPrinciple; or\n\n(b) a specified organisation had breached an approved privacy\ncode or a National Privacy Principle.\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate under subsection (1) or (2)\nmust, unless the contrary is established, be taken to be a certificate\nand to have been properly given.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-55b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-55b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-55b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-55b-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a5e8899434265b72a9cfd22db2ba3cc54aa5debbf74b02386c9a20c311db20d8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-55b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55B Evidentiary certificate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commissioner may issue a written certificate setting out the\nfindings of fact upon which the Commissioner based his or her\ndetermination that:\n\n(a) a specified agency had breached an Information Privacy\nPrinciple; or\n\n(b) a specified organisation had breached an approved privacy\ncode or a National Privacy Principle.\n\n(2) An adjudicator for an approved privacy code may issue a written\ncertificate setting out the findings of fact upon which the\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\nadjudicator based his or her determination that a specified\norganisation had breached an approved privacy code.\n\n(3) In any proceedings under section 55A, a certificate under\nsubsection (1) or (2) of this section is prima facie evidence of the\nfacts found by the Commissioner or adjudicator and set out in the\ncertificate. However, the certificate is not prima facie evidence of a\nfinding that:\n\n(a) a specified agency had breached an Information Privacy\nPrinciple; or\n\n(b) a specified organisation had breached an approved privacy\ncode or a National Privacy Principle.\n\n(4) A document purporting to be a certificate under subsection (1) or (2)\nmust, unless the contrary is established, be taken to be a certificate\nand to have been properly given."
    },
