    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-111",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "111 After subsection 68(3)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-111"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(3A) Before obtaining the consent, the authorised person must inform\nthe occupier or person in charge that he or she may refuse to\nconsent.\n\n(3B) An entry by an authorised person with the consent of the occupier\nor person in charge is not lawful if the consent was not voluntary.\n\n(3C) The authorised person may not enter premises (other than premises\noccupied by an agency) if:\n\n(a) the occupant or person in charge asks the authorised person\nto produce his or her identity card; and\n\n(b) the authorised person does not produce it.\n\n(3D) If an authorised person is on premises with the consent of the\noccupier or person in charge, the authorised person must leave the\npremises if the occupier or person in charge asks the authorised\nperson to do so.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(3A) Before obtaining the consent, the authorised person must inform\nthe occupier or person in charge that he or she may refuse to\nconsent.\n\n(3B) An entry by an authorised person with the consent of the occupier\nor person in charge is not lawful if the consent was not voluntary.\n\n(3C) The authorised person may not enter premises (other than premises\noccupied by an agency) if:\n\n(a) the occupant or person in charge asks the authorised person\nto produce his or her identity card; and\n\n(b) the authorised person does not produce it.\n\n(3D) If an authorised person is on premises with the consent of the\noccupier or person in charge, the authorised person must leave the\npremises if the occupier or person in charge asks the authorised\nperson to do so.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-111-ss-3a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-111-ss-3b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-111-ss-3c"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-111-ss-3d"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8445d5cfe714f4491bdd7be3a32948e53e2a96ef2d6d75ca8d501fbc73a359c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-111",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "111 After subsection 68(3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(3A) Before obtaining the consent, the authorised person must inform\nthe occupier or person in charge that he or she may refuse to\nconsent.\n\n(3B) An entry by an authorised person with the consent of the occupier\nor person in charge is not lawful if the consent was not voluntary.\n\n(3C) The authorised person may not enter premises (other than premises\noccupied by an agency) if:\n\n(a) the occupant or person in charge asks the authorised person\nto produce his or her identity card; and\n\n(b) the authorised person does not produce it.\n\n(3D) If an authorised person is on premises with the consent of the\noccupier or person in charge, the authorised person must leave the\npremises if the occupier or person in charge asks the authorised\nperson to do so."
    },
