    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-70b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "70B Application of this Part to former organisations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-70b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.66",
      "values:originalText": "If an individual, body corporate, partnership, unincorporated\nassociation or trust ceases to be an organisation but continues to\nexist, this Part operates in relation to:\n\n(a) an act or practice of the organisation (while it was an\norganisation); and\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(b) the individual, body corporate, partnership, unincorporated\nassociation or trust;\nas if he, she or it were still (and had been at all relevant times) an\norganisation.\nExample 1: If an individual carrying on a business was not a small business\noperator, but later became one and remained alive:\n(a)\na complaint may be made under this Part about an act or practice\nof the individual in carrying on the business before he or she\nbecame a small business operator; and\n(b)\nthe complaint may be investigated (and further proceedings\ntaken) under this Part as though the individual were still an\norganisation.\nExample 2: A small business operator chooses under section 6EA to be treated as\nan organisation, but later revokes the choice. A complaint about an act\nor practice the operator engaged in while the choice was registered\nunder that section may be made and investigated under this Part as if\nthe operator were an organisation.",
      "skos:definition": "If an individual, body corporate, partnership, unincorporated\nassociation or trust ceases to be an organisation but continues to\nexist, this Part operates in relation to:\n\n(a) an act or practice of the organisation (while it was an\norganisation); and\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(b) the individual, body corporate, partnership, unincorporated\nassociation or trust;\nas if he, she or it were still (and had been at all relevant times) an\norganisation.\nExample 1: If an individual carrying on a business was not a small business\noperator, but later became one and remained alive:\n(a)\na complaint may be made under this Part about an act or practice\nof the individual in carrying on the business before he or she\nbecame a small business operator; and\n(b)\nthe complaint may be investigated (and further proceedings\ntaken) under this Part as though the individual were still an\norganisation.\nExample 2: A small business operator chooses under section 6EA to be treated as\nan organisation, but later revokes the choice. A complaint about an act\nor practice the operator engaged in while the choice was registered\nunder that section may be made and investigated under this Part as if\nthe operator were an organisation.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-70b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-70b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9f0d8156106a1484a7fa386b058a43ef692ac3ec702c21a5ecd28f484591450d",
      "skos:note": "This Part operates in relation to an act or practice of the organisation (while it was an organisation); and the individual, body corporate, partnership, unincorporated association or trust; as if he, she or it were still (and had been at all relevant times) an organisation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-70b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "70B Application of this Part to former organisations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 66,
      "values:originalText": "If an individual, body corporate, partnership, unincorporated\nassociation or trust ceases to be an organisation but continues to\nexist, this Part operates in relation to:\n\n(a) an act or practice of the organisation (while it was an\norganisation); and\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(b) the individual, body corporate, partnership, unincorporated\nassociation or trust;\nas if he, she or it were still (and had been at all relevant times) an\norganisation.\nExample 1: If an individual carrying on a business was not a small business\noperator, but later became one and remained alive:\n(a)\na complaint may be made under this Part about an act or practice\nof the individual in carrying on the business before he or she\nbecame a small business operator; and\n(b)\nthe complaint may be investigated (and further proceedings\ntaken) under this Part as though the individual were still an\norganisation.\nExample 2: A small business operator chooses under section 6EA to be treated as\nan organisation, but later revokes the choice. A complaint about an act\nor practice the operator engaged in while the choice was registered\nunder that section may be made and investigated under this Part as if\nthe operator were an organisation."
    },
