    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-118",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "118 At the end of section 72",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-118"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.67",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nDeterminations about an organisation’s acts and practices\n\n(2) Subject to this Division, if the Commissioner is satisfied that:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(a) an act or practice of an organisation breaches, or may breach,\nan approved privacy code, or a National Privacy Principle,\nthat binds the organisation; but\n\n(b) the public interest in the organisation doing the act, or\nengaging in the practice, substantially outweighs the public\ninterest in adhering to that code or Principle;\nthe Commissioner may make a written determination to that effect.\nEffect of determination under subsection (2)\n\n(3) The organisation is taken not to contravene section 16A if the\norganisation does the act, or engages in the practice, while the\ndetermination is in force under subsection (2).\nGiving a determination under subsection (2) general effect\n\n(4) The Commissioner may make a written determination that no\norganisation is taken to contravene section 16A if, while that\ndetermination is in force, an organisation does an act, or engages in\na practice, that is the subject of a determination under\nsubsection (2) in relation to that organisation or any other\norganisation.\nEffect of determination under subsection (4)\n\n(5) A determination under subsection (4) has effect according to its\nterms.\nNote:\nThe following heading to subsection 72(1) is inserted “Determinations about an\nagency’s acts and practices”.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\nDeterminations about an organisation’s acts and practices\n\n(2) Subject to this Division, if the Commissioner is satisfied that:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(a) an act or practice of an organisation breaches, or may breach,\nan approved privacy code, or a National Privacy Principle,\nthat binds the organisation; but\n\n(b) the public interest in the organisation doing the act, or\nengaging in the practice, substantially outweighs the public\ninterest in adhering to that code or Principle;\nthe Commissioner may make a written determination to that effect.\nEffect of determination under subsection (2)\n\n(3) The organisation is taken not to contravene section 16A if the\norganisation does the act, or engages in the practice, while the\ndetermination is in force under subsection (2).\nGiving a determination under subsection (2) general effect\n\n(4) The Commissioner may make a written determination that no\norganisation is taken to contravene section 16A if, while that\ndetermination is in force, an organisation does an act, or engages in\na practice, that is the subject of a determination under\nsubsection (2) in relation to that organisation or any other\norganisation.\nEffect of determination under subsection (4)\n\n(5) A determination under subsection (4) has effect according to its\nterms.\nNote:\nThe following heading to subsection 72(1) is inserted “Determinations about an\nagency’s acts and practices”.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-118-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-118-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-118-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-118-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9f6a88aebced29c2baf14f84325f1af583d18d286270e1db444e98bf17859e11"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-118",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "118 At the end of section 72",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 67,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nDeterminations about an organisation’s acts and practices\n\n(2) Subject to this Division, if the Commissioner is satisfied that:\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(a) an act or practice of an organisation breaches, or may breach,\nan approved privacy code, or a National Privacy Principle,\nthat binds the organisation; but\n\n(b) the public interest in the organisation doing the act, or\nengaging in the practice, substantially outweighs the public\ninterest in adhering to that code or Principle;\nthe Commissioner may make a written determination to that effect.\nEffect of determination under subsection (2)\n\n(3) The organisation is taken not to contravene section 16A if the\norganisation does the act, or engages in the practice, while the\ndetermination is in force under subsection (2).\nGiving a determination under subsection (2) general effect\n\n(4) The Commissioner may make a written determination that no\norganisation is taken to contravene section 16A if, while that\ndetermination is in force, an organisation does an act, or engages in\na practice, that is the subject of a determination under\nsubsection (2) in relation to that organisation or any other\norganisation.\nEffect of determination under subsection (4)\n\n(5) A determination under subsection (4) has effect according to its\nterms.\nNote:\nThe following heading to subsection 72(1) is inserted “Determinations about an\nagency’s acts and practices”."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-118-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "118(2) At the end of section 72",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-118-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
