    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80A Temporary public interest determinations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-80a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the Commissioner is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the act or practice of an agency or organisation that is the\nsubject of an application under section 73 for a determination\nunder section 72 breaches, or may breach:\n\n(i) in the case of an agency—an Information Privacy\nPrinciple; and\n\n(ii) in the case of an organisation—an approved privacy\ncode, or a National Privacy Principle, that binds the\norganisation; and\n\n(b) the public interest in the agency or organisation doing the act,\nor engaging in the practice, outweighs to a substantial degree\nthe public interest in adhering to that Principle or code; and\n\n(c) the application raises issues that require an urgent decision.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may make a written temporary public interest\ndetermination that he or she is satisfied of the matters set out in\nsubsection (1). The Commissioner may do so:\n\n(a) on request by the agency or organisation; or\n\n(b) on the Commissioner’s own initiative.\n\n(3) The Commissioner must:\n\n(a) specify in the determination a period of up to 12 months\nduring which the determination is in force (subject to\nsubsection 80D(2)); and\n\n(b) include in the determination a statement of the reasons for the\ndetermination.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the Commissioner is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the act or practice of an agency or organisation that is the\nsubject of an application under section 73 for a determination\nunder section 72 breaches, or may breach:\n\n(i) in the case of an agency—an Information Privacy\nPrinciple; and\n\n(ii) in the case of an organisation—an approved privacy\ncode, or a National Privacy Principle, that binds the\norganisation; and\n\n(b) the public interest in the agency or organisation doing the act,\nor engaging in the practice, outweighs to a substantial degree\nthe public interest in adhering to that Principle or code; and\n\n(c) the application raises issues that require an urgent decision.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may make a written temporary public interest\ndetermination that he or she is satisfied of the matters set out in\nsubsection (1). The Commissioner may do so:\n\n(a) on request by the agency or organisation; or\n\n(b) on the Commissioner’s own initiative.\n\n(3) The Commissioner must:\n\n(a) specify in the determination a period of up to 12 months\nduring which the determination is in force (subject to\nsubsection 80D(2)); and\n\n(b) include in the determination a statement of the reasons for the\ndetermination.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80a-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8771907e6c525022c09226573ffe1a32c8727944e977fd47e08ef9fb37c4bbdb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-80a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80A Temporary public interest determinations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 70,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the Commissioner is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the act or practice of an agency or organisation that is the\nsubject of an application under section 73 for a determination\nunder section 72 breaches, or may breach:\n\n(i) in the case of an agency—an Information Privacy\nPrinciple; and\n\n(ii) in the case of an organisation—an approved privacy\ncode, or a National Privacy Principle, that binds the\norganisation; and\n\n(b) the public interest in the agency or organisation doing the act,\nor engaging in the practice, outweighs to a substantial degree\nthe public interest in adhering to that Principle or code; and\n\n(c) the application raises issues that require an urgent decision.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may make a written temporary public interest\ndetermination that he or she is satisfied of the matters set out in\nsubsection (1). The Commissioner may do so:\n\n(a) on request by the agency or organisation; or\n\n(b) on the Commissioner’s own initiative.\n\n(3) The Commissioner must:\n\n(a) specify in the determination a period of up to 12 months\nduring which the determination is in force (subject to\nsubsection 80D(2)); and\n\n(b) include in the determination a statement of the reasons for the\ndetermination.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1"
    },
