    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80D Commissioner may continue to consider application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-80d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.71",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The fact that the Commissioner has made a determination under\nthis Division about an act or practice does not prevent the\nCommissioner from dealing under Division 1 with an application\nmade under section 73 in relation to that act or practice.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(2) A determination under this Division about an act or practice ceases\nto be in effect when:\n\n(a) a determination made under subsection 72(1) or (2) (as\nappropriate) about the act or practice comes into effect; or\n\n(b) a determination is made under paragraph 78(b) to dismiss the\napplication.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The fact that the Commissioner has made a determination under\nthis Division about an act or practice does not prevent the\nCommissioner from dealing under Division 1 with an application\nmade under section 73 in relation to that act or practice.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(2) A determination under this Division about an act or practice ceases\nto be in effect when:\n\n(a) a determination made under subsection 72(1) or (2) (as\nappropriate) about the act or practice comes into effect; or\n\n(b) a determination is made under paragraph 78(b) to dismiss the\napplication.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-80d-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "09d26c91c9fbe551d8eaf292374f1b1d70b90279eced58f668bf685b23d8bbd3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-80d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80D Commissioner may continue to consider application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 71,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The fact that the Commissioner has made a determination under\nthis Division about an act or practice does not prevent the\nCommissioner from dealing under Division 1 with an application\nmade under section 73 in relation to that act or practice.\n\nSchedule 1  Amendment of the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(2) A determination under this Division about an act or practice ceases\nto be in effect when:\n\n(a) a determination made under subsection 72(1) or (2) (as\nappropriate) about the act or practice comes into effect; or\n\n(b) a determination is made under paragraph 78(b) to dismiss the\napplication."
    },
