    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-95b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "95B Requirements for Commonwealth contracts",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-95b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section requires an agency entering into a Commonwealth\ncontract to take contractual measures to ensure that a contracted\nservice provider for the contract does not do an act, or engage in a\npractice, that would breach an Information Privacy Principle if\ndone or engaged in by the agency.\n\n(2) The agency must ensure that the Commonwealth contract does not\nauthorise a contracted service provider for the contract to do or\nengage in such an act or practice.\n\n(3) The agency must also ensure that the Commonwealth contract\ncontains provisions to ensure that such an act or practice is not\nauthorised by a subcontract.\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), a subcontract is a contract\nunder which a contracted service provider for the Commonwealth\ncontract is engaged to provide services to:\n\n(a) another contracted service provider for the Commonwealth\ncontract; or\n\n(b) any agency;\nfor the purposes (whether direct or indirect) of the Commonwealth\ncontract.\n\n(5) This section applies whether the agency is entering into the\nCommonwealth contract on behalf of the Commonwealth or in the\nagency’s own right.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section requires an agency entering into a Commonwealth\ncontract to take contractual measures to ensure that a contracted\nservice provider for the contract does not do an act, or engage in a\npractice, that would breach an Information Privacy Principle if\ndone or engaged in by the agency.\n\n(2) The agency must ensure that the Commonwealth contract does not\nauthorise a contracted service provider for the contract to do or\nengage in such an act or practice.\n\n(3) The agency must also ensure that the Commonwealth contract\ncontains provisions to ensure that such an act or practice is not\nauthorised by a subcontract.\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), a subcontract is a contract\nunder which a contracted service provider for the Commonwealth\ncontract is engaged to provide services to:\n\n(a) another contracted service provider for the Commonwealth\ncontract; or\n\n(b) any agency;\nfor the purposes (whether direct or indirect) of the Commonwealth\ncontract.\n\n(5) This section applies whether the agency is entering into the\nCommonwealth contract on behalf of the Commonwealth or in the\nagency’s own right.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-95b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-95b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-95b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-95b-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-95b-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "68a40a7d6542402236454cf8e92c17f140d94c32a0096abf01a4940105a6d5c2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-95b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "95B Requirements for Commonwealth contracts",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section requires an agency entering into a Commonwealth\ncontract to take contractual measures to ensure that a contracted\nservice provider for the contract does not do an act, or engage in a\npractice, that would breach an Information Privacy Principle if\ndone or engaged in by the agency.\n\n(2) The agency must ensure that the Commonwealth contract does not\nauthorise a contracted service provider for the contract to do or\nengage in such an act or practice.\n\n(3) The agency must also ensure that the Commonwealth contract\ncontains provisions to ensure that such an act or practice is not\nauthorised by a subcontract.\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), a subcontract is a contract\nunder which a contracted service provider for the Commonwealth\ncontract is engaged to provide services to:\n\n(a) another contracted service provider for the Commonwealth\ncontract; or\n\n(b) any agency;\nfor the purposes (whether direct or indirect) of the Commonwealth\ncontract.\n\n(5) This section applies whether the agency is entering into the\nCommonwealth contract on behalf of the Commonwealth or in the\nagency’s own right.\n\nAmendment of the Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1"
    },
