      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(2A) The report must also include a statement about the operation of\napproved privacy codes that contain procedures for making and\ndealing with complaints in relation to acts or practices that may be\nan interference with the privacy of an individual, including:\n\n(a) action taken by adjudicators to monitor compliance with the\ncodes; and\n\n(b) details about the number of complaints made under codes,\ntheir nature and outcome.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(2A) The report must also include a statement about the operation of\napproved privacy codes that contain procedures for making and\ndealing with complaints in relation to acts or practices that may be\nan interference with the privacy of an individual, including:\n\n(a) action taken by adjudicators to monitor compliance with the\ncodes; and\n\n(b) details about the number of complaints made under codes,\ntheir nature and outcome.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-133-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-1-sec-133-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3ddf47befd09f9d99de2f6b0bce8bb93871b424be078e6af511a4241c7560e3a",
      "skos:note": "Report must include statement about approved privacy codes and their operation.",
      "dc:description": "Details about complaints made under codes, their nature and outcome."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-1-sec-133",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "133 After subsection 97(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(2A) The report must also include a statement about the operation of\napproved privacy codes that contain procedures for making and\ndealing with complaints in relation to acts or practices that may be\nan interference with the privacy of an individual, including:\n\n(a) action taken by adjudicators to monitor compliance with the\ncodes; and\n\n(b) details about the number of complaints made under codes,\ntheir nature and outcome."
    },
