    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must operate in relation to personal information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Collection of personal information from related body corporate",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Organisation must operate in relation to personal information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 4 Despite subclause 2.1, an organisation that provides a health",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-3-sec-2-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "service to an individual may disclose health information about the\nindividual to a person who is responsible for the individual if:\n\n(a) the individual:\n\n(i) is physically or legally incapable of giving consent to\nthe disclosure; or\n\n(ii) physically cannot communicate consent to the\ndisclosure; and\n\n(b) a natural person (the carer) providing the health service for\nthe organisation is satisfied that either:\n\n(i) the disclosure is necessary to provide appropriate care\nor treatment of the individual; or\n\n(ii) the disclosure is made for compassionate reasons; and\n\n(c) the disclosure is not contrary to any wish:\n\n(i) expressed by the individual before the individual\nbecame unable to give or communicate consent; and\n\n(ii) of which the carer is aware, or of which the carer could\nreasonably be expected to be aware; and\n\n(d) the disclosure is limited to the extent reasonable and\nnecessary for a purpose mentioned in paragraph (b).",
      "skos:definition": "service to an individual may disclose health information about the\nindividual to a person who is responsible for the individual if:\n\n(a) the individual:\n\n(i) is physically or legally incapable of giving consent to\nthe disclosure; or\n\n(ii) physically cannot communicate consent to the\ndisclosure; and\n\n(b) a natural person (the carer) providing the health service for\nthe organisation is satisfied that either:\n\n(i) the disclosure is necessary to provide appropriate care\nor treatment of the individual; or\n\n(ii) the disclosure is made for compassionate reasons; and\n\n(c) the disclosure is not contrary to any wish:\n\n(i) expressed by the individual before the individual\nbecame unable to give or communicate consent; and\n\n(ii) of which the carer is aware, or of which the carer could\nreasonably be expected to be aware; and\n\n(d) the disclosure is limited to the extent reasonable and\nnecessary for a purpose mentioned in paragraph (b).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-logic-argumentation-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e687b514f34bc7a9a12a59c529d03aa35b6a31d772d937ad8e6772a9a5550114",
      "skos:note": "Disclosure of health information under certain circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-3-sec-2-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 4 Despite subclause 2.1, an organisation that provides a health",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "service to an individual may disclose health information about the\nindividual to a person who is responsible for the individual if:\n\n(a) the individual:\n\n(i) is physically or legally incapable of giving consent to\nthe disclosure; or\n\n(ii) physically cannot communicate consent to the\ndisclosure; and\n\n(b) a natural person (the carer) providing the health service for\nthe organisation is satisfied that either:\n\n(i) the disclosure is necessary to provide appropriate care\nor treatment of the individual; or\n\n(ii) the disclosure is made for compassionate reasons; and\n\n(c) the disclosure is not contrary to any wish:\n\n(i) expressed by the individual before the individual\nbecame unable to give or communicate consent; and\n\n(ii) of which the carer is aware, or of which the carer could\nreasonably be expected to be aware; and\n\n(d) the disclosure is limited to the extent reasonable and\nnecessary for a purpose mentioned in paragraph (b)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Necessity",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The organisation has an obligation to disclose health information under certain circumstances.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "the individual is physically or legally incapable of giving consent to the disclosure;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the organisation must disclose health information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The disclosure must be limited to the extent reasonable and necessary for a purpose mentioned in paragraph (b).",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "the disclosure is not contrary to any wish:\n\n(i) expressed by the individual before the individual became unable to give or communicate consent; and\n\n(ii) of which the carer is aware, or of which the carer could reasonably be expected to be aware;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the disclosure must be limited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The disclosure must not continue beyond the point where the individual is able to give consent or communicate effectively.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "the individual is physically or legally incapable of giving consent to the disclosure;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the disclosure must stop when the individual is able to give consent or communicate effectively."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-logic-diffusion-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Propagation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The disclosure of health information may lead to further disclosures under certain circumstances.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "a natural person providing the health service for the organisation is satisfied that either:\n\n(i) the disclosure is necessary to provide appropriate care or treatment of the individual; or\n\n(ii) the disclosure is made for compassionate reasons;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the disclosure may lead to further disclosures."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-5-logic-argumentation-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implication",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The organisation's decision to disclose health information implies that it has considered the potential consequences and alternatives.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "a natural person providing the health service for the organisation is satisfied that either:\n\n(i) the disclosure is necessary to provide appropriate care or treatment of the individual; or\n\n(ii) the disclosure is made for compassionate reasons;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the organisation's decision implies consideration of potential consequences and alternatives."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Section 2",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-3-sec-2-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "5 For the purposes of subclause 2.4, a person is responsible for an\nindividual if the person is:\n\n(a) a parent of the individual; or\n\n(b) a child or sibling of the individual and at least 18 years old;\nor\n\n(c) a spouse or de facto spouse of the individual; or\n\n(d) a relative of the individual, at least 18 years old and a\nmember of the individual’s household; or\n\n(e) a guardian of the individual; or\n\n(f) exercising an enduring power of attorney granted by the\nindividual that is exercisable in relation to decisions about\nthe individual’s health; or\n\n(g) a person who has an intimate personal relationship with the\nindividual; or\n\n(h) a person nominated by the individual to be contacted in case\nof emergency.",
      "skos:definition": "5 For the purposes of subclause 2.4, a person is responsible for an\nindividual if the person is:\n\n(a) a parent of the individual; or\n\n(b) a child or sibling of the individual and at least 18 years old;\nor\n\n(c) a spouse or de facto spouse of the individual; or\n\n(d) a relative of the individual, at least 18 years old and a\nmember of the individual’s household; or\n\n(e) a guardian of the individual; or\n\n(f) exercising an enduring power of attorney granted by the\nindividual that is exercisable in relation to decisions about\nthe individual’s health; or\n\n(g) a person who has an intimate personal relationship with the\nindividual; or\n\n(h) a person nominated by the individual to be contacted in case\nof emergency.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-3-sec-2-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "953743e01095a68c7eb2f2de61c625b31d1bca7c0481dc2a05bfb5ee95dfcc0f",
      "skos:note": "Person responsible for an individual"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-3-sec-2-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Section 2",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "5 For the purposes of subclause 2.4, a person is responsible for an\nindividual if the person is:\n\n(a) a parent of the individual; or\n\n(b) a child or sibling of the individual and at least 18 years old;\nor\n\n(c) a spouse or de facto spouse of the individual; or\n\n(d) a relative of the individual, at least 18 years old and a\nmember of the individual’s household; or\n\n(e) a guardian of the individual; or\n\n(f) exercising an enduring power of attorney granted by the\nindividual that is exercisable in relation to decisions about\nthe individual’s health; or\n\n(g) a person who has an intimate personal relationship with the\nindividual; or\n\n(h) a person nominated by the individual to be contacted in case\nof emergency."
    },
    {
