    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-2-sec-303c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "303C Prosecution of an offence against this Part does not affect",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-2-sec-303c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000.pdf, p.92",
      "values:originalText": "proceedings under the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(1) The prosecution of an offence against Division 2 or 4 of this Part\nfor disclosure or use of information or a document does not prevent\ncivil proceedings or administrative action from being taken under\nthe Privacy Act 1988 or an approved privacy code (as defined in\nthat Act) in relation to the disclosure or use.\n\n(2) This section applies regardless of the outcome of the prosecution.\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 2\n\n(3) This section does not affect the operation of section 49 of the\nPrivacy Act 1988.",
      "skos:definition": "proceedings under the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(1) The prosecution of an offence against Division 2 or 4 of this Part\nfor disclosure or use of information or a document does not prevent\ncivil proceedings or administrative action from being taken under\nthe Privacy Act 1988 or an approved privacy code (as defined in\nthat Act) in relation to the disclosure or use.\n\n(2) This section applies regardless of the outcome of the prosecution.\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 2\n\n(3) This section does not affect the operation of section 49 of the\nPrivacy Act 1988.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-2-sec-303c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-2-sec-303c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000-sch-2-sec-303c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e5c05181f53aa68b91e2bc6922da9599382cd54cd9b9e13aa57fdb361b7d6d31"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-amendment-private-sector-act-2000#sch-2-sec-303c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "303C Prosecution of an offence against this Part does not affect",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 92,
      "values:originalText": "proceedings under the Privacy Act 1988\n\n(1) The prosecution of an offence against Division 2 or 4 of this Part\nfor disclosure or use of information or a document does not prevent\ncivil proceedings or administrative action from being taken under\nthe Privacy Act 1988 or an approved privacy code (as defined in\nthat Act) in relation to the disclosure or use.\n\n(2) This section applies regardless of the outcome of the prosecution.\n\nAmendment of other Acts  Schedule 2\n\n(3) This section does not affect the operation of section 49 of the\nPrivacy Act 1988."
    },
